WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:30.083


2
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:34.250
<b>Here Lord Krishna advances the</b>
<b>concept of the soul's immortality</b>

3
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.875
<b>and says,</b>

4
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:37.708
<b>those who think that</b>

5
00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:40.166
<b>the soul can kill someone,</b>

6
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.250
<b>or that the soul itself can die,</b>

7
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.458
<b>both are ignorant.</b>

8
00:00:45.458 --> 00:00:48.041
<b>Because the soul neither kills</b>

9
00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:50.666
<b>nor dies</b>

10
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:55.583


11
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:57.791
<b>Think about it this way.</b>

12
00:00:57.791 --> 00:00:59.708
<b>The soul is eternal,</b>

13
00:00:59.708 --> 00:01:02.208
<b>it will remain even after the body's destruction,</b>

14
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:03.625
<b>it won't die.</b>

15
00:01:03.625 --> 00:01:05.416
<b>So if it never dies,</b>

16
00:01:05.416 --> 00:01:09.041
<b>how can there be any question of</b>
<b>someone killing it?</b>

17
00:01:09.041 --> 00:01:11.791
<b>Therefore, Lord Krishna says here that</b>

18
00:01:11.791 --> 00:01:17.875
<b>both these thoughts</b>
<b>that the soul can die or can kill - are wrong.</b>

19
00:01:17.875 --> 00:01:22.458
<b>Krishna is trying to</b>
<b>address Arjuna's concern here.</b>

20
00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:23.750
<b>Arjuna was worried</b>

21
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.125
<b>that if he kills his kinsmen in battle,</b>

22
00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:35.041
<b>some might say that Arjuna too killed his</b>
<b>relatives and teacher for the kingdom,</b>

23
00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:37.625
<b>so this must be right,</b>

24
00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:42.291
<b>and following this belief, they might take</b>
<b>the wrong path of unrighteousness.</b>

25
00:01:42.291 --> 00:01:44.958
<b>In response to this, Krishna says</b>

26
00:01:44.958 --> 00:01:50.041
<b>that if anyone thinks that you killed someone,</b>
<b>or someone died,</b>

27
00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:52.041
<b>they are ignorant.</b>

28
00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:58.125
<b>And don't let such ignorant people's imaginary</b>
<b>thoughts affect your duty.</b>

29
00:01:58.125 --> 00:01:59.708
<b>But perhaps</b>

30
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:04.583
<b>this might raise a question in someone's mind.</b>

31
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:07.125
<b>What about a murderer then?</b>

32
00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:12.625
<b>If no one kills and no one dies,</b>
<b>then is murder also acceptable?</b>

33
00:02:12.625 --> 00:02:16.541
<b>Should murderers not be punished?</b>

34
00:02:16.541 --> 00:02:17.750
<b>Wait, wait,</b>

35
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.375
<b>let's understand this.</b>

36
00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:20.958
<b>Sometimes knowingly,</b>

37
00:02:20.958 --> 00:02:22.541
<b>sometimes in ignorance,</b>

38
00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:25.541
<b>this is the mistake humans often make</b>

39
00:02:25.541 --> 00:02:27.583
<b>without understanding the</b>
<b>complete knowledge,</b>

40
00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:30.625
<b>they take just one part of it and,</b>

41
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:38.250
<b>according to their convenience, try to justify</b>
<b>their actions by making it their argument.</b>

42
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.916
<b>Try to understand this from this perspective</b>

43
00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:44.750
<b>is Arjuna fighting for dharma here,</b>

44
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.333
<b>or for selfishness?</b>

45
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:47.500
<b>For dharma,</b>

46
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.541
<b>right?</b>

47
00:02:48.541 --> 00:02:52.708
<b>Because if it were selfishness,</b>
<b>his mind wouldn't be so disturbed.</b>

48
00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:53.916
<b>And secondly,</b>

49
00:02:53.916 --> 00:02:59.458
<b>isn't Arjuna making every possible effort</b>
<b>to avoid having to raise weapons,</b>

50
00:02:59.458 --> 00:03:01.666
<b>which might take lives?</b>

51
00:03:01.666 --> 00:03:04.083
<b>He was talking about dying himself,</b>

52
00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.916
<b>about begging for alms again.</b>

53
00:03:06.916 --> 00:03:07.625
<b>But</b>

54
00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:13.333
<b>even after all this, after all this thinking,</b>
<b>the war won't be averted, will it?</b>

55
00:03:13.333 --> 00:03:15.708
<b>And if Duryodhana wins the war,</b>

56
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:18.750
<b>who knows how many Draupadis</b>
<b>will be dishonored,</b>

57
00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.791
<b>how much unrighteousness will spread.</b>

58
00:03:20.791 --> 00:03:21.666
<b>In such a situation,</b>

59
00:03:21.666 --> 00:03:24.625
<b>now there is no way except war,</b>

60
00:03:24.625 --> 00:03:28.250
<b>raising weapons is the last resort.</b>

61
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:30.916
<b>Would a murderer think this much?</b>

62
00:03:30.916 --> 00:03:33.708
<b>Does he kill for society's welfare,</b>

63
00:03:33.708 --> 00:03:35.250
<b>or for his selfishness,</b>

64
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.458
<b>or after completely losing control in anger?</b>

65
00:03:39.458 --> 00:03:42.875
<b>It's necessary that we understand</b>
<b>Arjuna's situation.</b>

66
00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:44.791
<b>Understand the complete Gita.</b>

67
00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.125
<b>Understand the essence of this knowledge.</b>

68
00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:52.208
<b>And never misuse this knowledge</b>
<b>for unrighteousness.</b>

69
00:03:52.916 --> 00:03:57.166


70
00:03:57.166 --> 00:03:59.500
<b>"I achieved this success."</b>

71
00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:06.291
<b>"This accomplishment is the result</b>
<b>of my hard work."</b>

72
00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:08.958
<b>Some phrases spoken by humans,</b>

73
00:04:08.958 --> 00:04:10.416
<b>especially when</b>

74
00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:14.958
<b>they achieve success.</b>

75
00:04:14.958 --> 00:04:16.291
<b>But</b>

76
00:04:16.291 --> 00:04:18.083
<b>is this true?</b>

77
00:04:18.083 --> 00:04:22.833
<b>Is our success solely the work of our hands?</b>

78
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:30.041
<b>Or is this success formed by many other things,</b>
<b>coincidences coming together?</b>

79
00:04:30.041 --> 00:04:31.958
<b>You stood first in an exam</b>

80
00:04:31.958 --> 00:04:37.375
<b>your effort certainly makes</b>
<b>a significant contribution,</b>

81
00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:38.416
<b>but</b>

82
00:04:38.416 --> 00:04:41.500
<b>it also depends on the question paper.</b>

83
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:48.500
<b>It depends on whether perhaps others</b>
<b>couldn't perform well that day.</b>

84
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.875
<b>This is just one example.</b>

85
00:04:50.875 --> 00:04:53.166
<b>If you observe carefully,</b>

86
00:04:53.166 --> 00:04:57.875
<b>you'll see the hand of many other</b>
<b>circumstances in each of your results.</b>

87
00:04:57.875 --> 00:04:58.791
<b>Perhaps</b>

88
00:04:58.791 --> 00:05:00.916
<b>other people too.</b>

89
00:05:00.916 --> 00:05:03.833
<b>It's necessary to understand this perspective.</b>

90
00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:05.375
<b>That what is happening</b>

91
00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:08.541
<b>our part in it is extremely important,</b>

92
00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.208
<b>but</b>

93
00:05:10.208 --> 00:05:14.875
<b>taking complete credit would be a mistake.</b>

94
00:05:14.875 --> 00:05:16.916
<b>Similarly is this knowledge</b>

95
00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.958
<b>that the soul neither dies</b>

96
00:05:18.958 --> 00:05:21.333
<b>nor kills.</b>

97
00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:28.000
<b>Understanding the complete essence of</b>
<b>this statement might take more time.</b>

98
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.166
<b>It will be further illuminated in the</b>
<b>coming chapters of the Gita.</b>

99
00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.541
<b>But for now,</b>

100
00:05:34.541 --> 00:05:36.291
<b>grasp it this way</b>

101
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:41.250
<b>that in our actions, while our role is important,</b>

102
00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:47.583
<b>many other circumstances and</b>
<b>events also play their part.</b>

103
00:05:47.583 --> 00:05:49.291
<b>So to say</b>

104
00:05:49.291 --> 00:05:51.916
<b>"I alone did this"</b>

105
00:05:51.916 --> 00:05:54.125
<b>would be wrong.</b>

106
00:05:54.125 --> 00:05:58.833
<b>This understanding not only encourages</b>
<b>you to perform your duties</b>

107
00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:02.166
<b>but also keeps you humble.</b>

108
00:06:02.833 --> 00:06:06.708


109
00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:07.916
<b>to know that </b>

110
00:06:07.916 --> 00:06:09.333
<b>our loved ones,</b>

111
00:06:09.333 --> 00:06:10.791
<b>our family members,</b>

112
00:06:10.791 --> 00:06:15.500
<b>don't die even after leaving their bodies,</b>

113
00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:21.166
<b>How calming and liberating is this thought.</b>

114
00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:22.166
<b>Yes,</b>

115
00:06:22.166 --> 00:06:26.166
<b>in such times grief is natural,</b>

116
00:06:26.166 --> 00:06:26.916
<b>but</b>

117
00:06:26.916 --> 00:06:29.541
<b>this knowledge of the soul's infinity</b>

118
00:06:29.541 --> 00:06:35.416
<b>will surely help you recover from such sorrow.</b>

119
00:06:35.416 --> 00:06:36.958
<b>At the same time,</b>

120
00:06:36.958 --> 00:06:39.750
<b>some questions may arise in the mind.</b>

121
00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:43.500
<b>Where do we go after death?</b>

122
00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.416
<b>If death is not the end,</b>

123
00:06:45.416 --> 00:06:50.375
<b>then what is the destination of</b>
<b>our spiritual journey?</b>

124
00:06:50.375 --> 00:06:54.708
<b>Do we have any control over all this?</b>

125
00:06:54.708 --> 00:07:00.375
<b>Can we influence our spiritual future?</b>

126
00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:01.333
<b>This</b>

127
00:07:01.333 --> 00:07:03.375
<b>and many such questions,</b>

128
00:07:03.375 --> 00:07:06.333
<b>all have their answers in this Gita.</b>

129
00:07:06.333 --> 00:07:10.791
<b>Gradually everything will be revealed.</b>

130
00:07:10.791 --> 00:07:12.666
<b>Stay with us.</b>

131
00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.416


132
00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:21.000
<b>In life, sometimes we</b>
<b>make right decisions,</b>

133
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.458
<b>and sometimes we make wrong ones.</b>

134
00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:26.083
<b>Sometimes there is profit,</b>

135
00:07:26.083 --> 00:07:28.416
<b>and sometimes loss.</b>

136
00:07:28.416 --> 00:07:30.916
<b>Sometimes good things happen to us,</b>

137
00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:34.625
<b>and sometimes bad things are possible too.</b>

138
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:39.000
<b>All this is just a part of life.</b>

139
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.333
<b>The person who remains</b>
<b>absorbed only in materialism,</b>

140
00:07:42.333 --> 00:07:46.458
<b>who considers only worldly life as truth,</b>

141
00:07:46.458 --> 00:07:53.916
<b>keeps moving up and down like</b>
<b>an empty boat floating on waves.</b>

142
00:07:53.916 --> 00:07:56.875
<b>In sorrow they lament,</b>

143
00:07:56.875 --> 00:08:00.250
<b>and in good times they become arrogant.</b>

144
00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:06.416
<b>Victory feels to them like their right,</b>
<b>and they consider their defeat as life's injustice.</b>

145
00:08:06.416 --> 00:08:09.583
<b>Profit appears to them as the fruit of their work,</b>

146
00:08:09.583 --> 00:08:14.041
<b>and loss appears as someone else's mistake.</b>

147
00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:15.541
<b>But</b>

148
00:08:15.541 --> 00:08:18.416
<b>one who understands this knowledge of the Gita</b>

149
00:08:18.416 --> 00:08:20.583
<b>will remain humble in victory</b>

150
00:08:20.583 --> 00:08:23.625
<b>and patient in defeat.</b>

151
00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:29.291
<b>That person will stay balanced</b>
<b>in both happiness and sorrow, profit and loss.</b>

152
00:08:29.291 --> 00:08:30.125
<b>Because</b>

153
00:08:30.125 --> 00:08:31.708
<b>one who has understood</b>

154
00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:34.750
<b>that our real existence is the soul,</b>

155
00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:39.000
<b>and worldly events don't affect the soul,</b>

156
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:46.375
<b>that person will remain steady and</b>
<b>serene through all of life's ups and downs.</b>

